My life shattered after a traumatic incident that left me with severe short-term memory loss. My days reset without warning, forcing me to depend on written reminders just to survive.
I write everything down—dates, passwords, clues—on walls and inside files, turning my surroundings into a map of my fractured memory.
What I don’t know is that the person I’m trying to kill is the detective’s father. Hidden behind a mask and driven by distorted memories, I believe I’m finishing something I once started.

